{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ECC",
  "chapter": 4,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ECC.4.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.4.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So I returned, and considered all the oppressions that are done under the sun: and behold the tears of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "such as were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " oppressed, and they had no comforter; and on the side of their oppressors ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " power; but they had no comforter.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.4.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.4.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore I praised the dead who are already dead more than the living who are yet alive.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.4.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.4.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, better is ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " than both they, who hath not yet been, who hath not seen the evil work that is done under the sun.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.4.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.4.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Again, I considered all labor, and every right work, that for this a man is envied by his neighbor. This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " also vanity and vexation of spirit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.4.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.4.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The fool foldeth his hands together, and eateth his own flesh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.4.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.4.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Better ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a handful ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " quietness, than both the hands full ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " toil and vexation of spirit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.4.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.4.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then I returned, and I saw vanity under the sun.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.4.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.4.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is one ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "alone",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not a second; yes, he hath neither child nor brother: yet ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no end of all his labor; neither is his eye satisfied with riches; neither ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "saith he",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", For whom do I labor, and bereave my soul of good? This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " also vanity, yes, it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a grievous labor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.4.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.4.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Two ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " better than one; because they have a good reward for their labor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.4.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.4.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For if they fall, the one will lift up his fellow: but woe to him ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " alone when he falleth; for ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he hath",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not another to help him to rise.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.4.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.4.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Again, if two lie together, then they have heat: but how can one be warm ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "alone",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.4.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.4.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And if one prevaileth against him, two shall withstand him; and a three-fold cord is not quickly broken.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.4.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.4.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Better ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a poor and a wise child, than an old and foolish king, who will no more be admonished.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.4.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.4.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For out of prison he cometh to reign; whereas also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " born in his kingdom becometh poor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.4.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.4.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I considered all the living who walk under the sun, with the second child that shall stand up in his stead.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.4.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.4.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no end of all the people, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of all that have been before them: they also that come after shall not rejoice in him. Surely this also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vanity and vexation of spirit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
